            <div xml:id="d396">

                <pb facs="0623" n="537" sameAs="frus:frus1927v01/pg537"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.6362/18: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Collier</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-09-01T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 1,
                                1927—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 5:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>119. Government has sent to Congress proposed law to aid coal industry. It
                    provides for a Government coal board, imposes heavy increased duties on coal and
                    crude petroleum, creates fund for port <pb facs="0624" n="538" xml:id="pg538"/>
                    works and for loans not exceeding 20 million pesos to private persons for
                    construction of [colliers], grants annual subsidy of 10 pesos per ton of cargo
                    capacity for ships constructed in Chile and a mileage subsidy of 2 pesos per ton
                    of coal transported in Chilean vessels per 1,000 kilometers. Full text and
                    analysis of bill will reach you September 29th.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d396-f1"/>
                    This should be considered in connection with proposed ship subsidy law.<anchor
                        n="28" xml:id="d396-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Collier</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
